ad this ridiculous stunt in front of  a church and his Attorney General was  tear gassing people to get the  the way so he could pose for a picture  with the Bible that sort of thing just  incites more violence and it gives  people the feeling that their concerns  are unheard so his response has been  very very unhelpful but Obama when  Baltimore erupted after a man named  Freddie gray was killed by police he  called the protesters thugs so III think  it's important not to think of Trump as  being so different yeah I want you to  take a listen to what former President  Barack Obama said just last night take a  listen  just remember this country was founded  on protest it is called the American  Revolution and every step of progress in  this country every expansion of freedom  every expression of our deepest ideals  has been won through efforts that made  the status quo uncomfortable and and  then we should all be thankful for folks  who are willing in a peaceful  disciplined way to be out there making a  difference there the former president  says it's even a part of American  history to protest yes but that's just  Obama's platitudes it's uh you know  which seems to be the only thing he can  say these days I guess because he's not  president anymore he can't get the best  speech writers but and I'm being  sarcastic obviously nobody needs him to  tell us that we have the right to  peacefully assemble nobody needs him to  tell us that it is the people who have  always made positive change in this  country we know that but he for eight  years he had the power he had the  authority to get these killer cops there  was a man here in New York City named  Eric garner and like George Floyd his  last words were I can't breathe and the  Obama Justice Department did nothing to  that cop and all he got was finally fire  from his job it took four or five years  or even that to happen so we don't need  to hear from Barack Obama he really  needs to just sit this out what about a  